---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Services"
  description="Send me one product, a short list, or a buying problem. I'll check what fits, what looks wrong, and what the tradeoffs are."
>
  <div class="desk-page">
    <header class="desk-page-header">
      <p class="desk-eyebrow">The Buying Desk / services</p>
      <h1>Start with the decision.</h1>
      <p>
        Three remote, manual services. I'll confirm what I can check, how long
        it'll take, and the price by email before I start.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="desk-section" aria-labelledby="active-services">
      <div class="desk-section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="desk-kicker">Available now</p>
          <h2 id="active-services">Choose the closest fit.</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="desk-grid">
        <article class="desk-card">
          <p class="desk-code">Form A / single item</p>
          <h2>Check This</h2>
          <p>For one product, listing, or deal you’re already considering.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Fit for your intended use</li>
            <li>Price context and obvious red flags</li>
            <li>Seller questions and evidence to request</li>
            <li>A clear verdict with visible limits</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="desk-link" href="/request?service=check-this"
            >Start Check This →</a
          >
        </article>
        <article class="desk-card">
          <p class="desk-code">Form B / short list</p>
          <h2>Compare These</h2>
          <p>For two required options and an optional third.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Tradeoffs tied to your use</li>
            <li>Value, longevity, and repair considerations</li>
            <li>What each option does better or worse</li>
            <li>A recommendation, not a spec dump</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="desk-link" href="/request?service=compare-these"
            >Start Compare These →</a
          >
        </article>
        <article class="desk-card">
          <p class="desk-code">Form C / open search</p>
          <h2>Choose for Me</h2>
          <p>For a job and budget without a settled shortlist.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>A small short list that actually fits</li>
            <li>Region and currency considered</li>
            <li>Deal-breakers kept visible</li>
            <li>Clear compromises at the budget</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="desk-link" href="/request?service=choose-for-me"
            >Start Choose for Me →</a
          >
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="desk-section" aria-labelledby="coverage-title">
      <div class="desk-section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="desk-kicker">Coverage</p>
          <h2 id="coverage-title">Broad category, honest boundary.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          I can help with laptops, tablets, keyboards, 3D printers, audio,
          phones, PC parts, home servers, and similar tech.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="desk-two-column">
        <article class="desk-card">
          <h3>What I can include</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Verdict and confidence</li>
            <li>Fair-price context where evidence allows</li>
            <li>Expected fit for the stated use</li>
            <li>Limitations, warning signs, and seller questions</li>
            <li>Requested tests or screenshots</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="desk-card unavailable">
          <p class="desk-code">Later / not available</p>
          <h3>Inspect It</h3>
          <p>
            I'm not doing in-person inspections during this pilot. If I havent
            touched the device, I wont pretend I did.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="desk-section desk-final">
      <h2>Not sure which one?</h2>
      <p>Pick the closest one. I can fix the scope when I reply.</p>
      <div class="desk-actions">
        <a class="desk-button" href="/request">Start a request</a>
        <a class="desk-button secondary" href="/how-it-works">How it works</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
